## Part B: the real-world cause of duplicates. worker-1 (sole consumer) processes
## order-0005 and records its event_id, then crashes BEFORE the ACK reaches the broker.
## RabbitMQ redelivers order-0005 to worker-2, which must detect it as a duplicate.

===== Part B merged timeline =====
22:05:29.666 [worker-1 pid=2681] waiting for messages on queue 'orders' (Ctrl+C to stop)
22:05:31.686 [worker-1 pid=2681] RECEIVED  event_id=7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1 order_id=order-0005 item_id=item-500 qty=3
22:05:31.686 [worker-1 pid=2681] PROCESSING order_id=order-0005 item_id=item-500 qty=3 ...
22:05:31.687 [producer] published {"event_id": "7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1", "order_id": "order-0005", "item_id": "item-500", "quantity": 3}
22:05:31.687 [producer] done: 1 message(s) published to queue 'orders'
22:05:32.115 [worker-2 pid=2690] waiting for messages on queue 'orders' (Ctrl+C to stop)
22:05:32.692 [worker-1 pid=2681] DONE      order_id=order-0005 processed
22:05:32.692 [worker-1 pid=2681] SIMULATED CRASH: work done but exiting before ACK for event_id=7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1 (redelivery will be a duplicate)
22:05:32.695 [worker-2 pid=2690] RECEIVED  event_id=7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1 order_id=order-0005 item_id=item-500 qty=3  [REDELIVERED]
22:05:32.696 [worker-2 pid=2690] DUPLICATE event_id=7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1 already processed -> skipping business action
22:05:32.697 [worker-2 pid=2690] ACK       event_id=7c2fd731-1c71-40a9-a5cf-ebd77cc904a1 (duplicate discarded)

